 The normal force is equal and opposite to the component of the gravitational force in the perpendicular direction. If the box has mass $m$, then the normal force $N$ and force due to gravity $mg$ can be written as follows in terms of the angle $\theta$:
\begin{align*}
N &= mg \cos \theta \\
mg &= mg \sin \theta \\
\end{align*}
We see from the equation for $N$ that if $\theta$ increases, then the normal force decreases, and that it decreases nonlinearly, because $\cos \theta$ is a nonlinear function of $\theta$. The answer is (E).
